  "findings": [
    "Across fixed input chunk sizes 1 through 22, the fix and v1.2.1 return permanent BROTLI_DECODER_ERROR_FORMAT_BLOCK_SWITCH (-17).",
    "The pre-fix parent returns BROTLI_DECODER_ERROR_FORMAT_HUFFMAN_SPACE (-9), demonstrating the status-semantic difference but not an out-of-bounds report.",
    "Every run preserved the harness guards. No AddressSanitizer diagnostic occurred; no memory-overwrite reproduction is claimed.",
    "The malformed stream can produce 16,777,216 or 16,777,218 provisional bytes before the permanent error depending on chunking, so callers must quarantine provisional output when complete-message validity is required."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "The Rust B2 component does not yet decode complete Brotli streams, so no native equivalence claim is made.",
    "FNV-1a is a compact run diagnostic; SHA-256 identities are used for sources and locally generated one-byte output artifacts, which are not committed.",
    "ASan can miss intra-object corruption; absence of an ASan report is not proof that the vulnerable parent is memory-safe.",
    "Benchmarks and broader valid/malformed corpus comparisons remain pending until a comparable Rust decoding path exists."
  ],
  "approved_on": "2026-10-24"
}
